{"content":[{"c":["BEER"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Israelite campsite on their wilderness journey, probably just north of the Arnon River on the Moabite-Amorite border (",{"href":"?bref=Num.21.16","r":"Num.21.16","rawR":"Num.21.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.21.16","value":"Num.21.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 21:16"},"). The name means “a well.” Water from the well they dug there was commemorated in a song (",{"href":"?bref=Num.21.17-18","r":"Num.21.17-18","rawR":"Num.21.17-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.21.17-18","value":"Num.21.17-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 21:17-18"},"). A Moabite well that was later called Beer-elim (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.15.8","r":"Isa.15.8","rawR":"Isa.15.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.15.8","value":"Isa.15.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 15:8"},") may have been the same location. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Wilderness Wanderings"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Place to which Gideon’s son Jotham escaped after telling a parable against his half brother Abimelech, who had killed all the other sons of Gideon in an attempt to become king of Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.9.21","r":"Judg.9.21","rawR":"Judg.9.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.9.21","value":"Judg.9.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 9:21"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Beer","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 21:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.21.16","rawQueryValue":"Num.21.16","sourceRefExact":"Num.21.16"},{"anchorText":"Nm 21:17-18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.21.17-18","rawQueryValue":"Num.21.17-18","sourceRefExact":"Num.21.17-18"},{"anchorText":"Is 15:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.15.8","rawQueryValue":"Isa.15.8","sourceRefExact":"Isa.15.8"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 9:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.9.21","rawQueryValue":"Judg.9.21","sourceRefExact":"Judg.9.21"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"53655bea65ba5f6438118103a97914f06006b94a82185905783073a5a5bf88df","sourceItemName":"Beer","sourceItemOrder":139,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Beer","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Beer","title":"Beer","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}